WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:03.070
The soul that used to be in this body
will likely never be at peace.

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:08.500
Further out is a planet
where intelligent lifeforms live...

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:11.400
...and here, people took the act
of giving birth...

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:14.850
...and raising children
far too much for granted.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:30.740
Father and Son

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:38.810
Are you saying that being brought up
on Earth isn't a good enough reason?

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:41.460
That's right. Take the red mobile suit
for example.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:45.590
That single unit has the power to influence
the movements of mobile suits in its vicinity.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.560
In order to counteract it...

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.120
...I'd like to ask you to compromise
your principles and policies...!

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.800
What are your thoughts on pursuing them
any further, Lieutenant Commander?

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:01.410
Our main problem is our shortage
of available mobile suits.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.880
However, we'd be at a loss to rebuild
our fighting power...

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.920
...and return for another battle.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:10.420
Continue the pursuit with
the Alexandria, Bosnia and Sichuan.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.710
And you, Captain?

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.760
I'll return to Gryps on the Brunei.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:15.960
Lieutenant Commander,
I'm relying on you...

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:18.000
...to find out where
the A.E.U.G.'s real base is.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.390
Shall we assault Granada?

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.660
Right now, our focus should be
in forcing out the A.E.U.G.'s sympathizers...

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:26.600
...who have penetrated
into the regular army.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:27.600
Yes, sir!

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:31.000
Show them no mercy.
Do as you wish with them.

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:35.170
Transfer the supplies from
the Brunei at once!

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:51.390
The Titans appear agitated by the loss
of the hostages and Gundam Mk. IIs.

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:55.290
In addition, I doubt they'd expect us
to launch an attack on them.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:56.520
Good point.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.540
One would normally expect us to return
to our hideout...

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:01.090
...upon capturing the Gundam Mk. IIs.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.270
I'd like to praise you on a clever plan...

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:06.040
...but do we have enough combat power,
Lieutenant Quattro Bajeena?

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:08.680
We'll use one Gundam Mk. II in our attack.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:12.710
Astonaige is overseeing the task
of painting them.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:13.980
Painting?

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.550
You don't want to leave them
in Titans' colors, do you?

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.650
How could you use it
in such an incorrect way?!

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:24.390
Before you take off that balancer...

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.020
...you must dislodge
all the surrounding insulation first!

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.070
Well, that's easy for you to say, but...!

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.330
A mechanic develops a sense
for these things.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.600
These guys hardly have any skill
at all!

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:34.600
You heard the man!
Now, get a move on, will you?!

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:41.170
Hey! I can't have you handling
the laser torch that way!

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:45.840
The heat conduction of that frame
is very quick.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.020
I'll show you how to use it.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:50.890
Lieutenant?!

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:55.690
Please take into account your position here.

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:59.350
I'm giving all my effort because
I'm keeping that in mind, Astonaige.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.070
Lower your guns!

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.540
I just want to have a look at the Rick Dias.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.200
As a fellow technician, that's all.

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:13.440
B-But!

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:15.870
This torch is capable of taking a life.

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:21.910
Don't move for five minutes!

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.220
I didn't believe you only intended to look at it.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.020
I'm returning with the Rick Dias.

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:30.620
Are you serious?

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:32.690
Bask held you hostage, remember?

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:34.730
So now he owes me one.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.790
In addition, if I brought him a Rick Dias...

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:41.630
I'll be free to do as I wish
at the Titans' technical division.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:42.870
Bastard!

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:45.170
Don't make me pull this trigger!

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:58.590
Thanks!

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:03.250
Argama! Catch me!

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:11.570
Impressive.

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:14.800
This 360 degree screen
is practically perfect.

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:22.440
What?!

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:24.350
<i>He's launching.</i>

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:25.970
Don't do anything while on the deck!

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:27.140
And hold your fire!

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:27.740
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:39.160
- What is it?!
- Have Roberto and Apolly go after him!

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:40.820
I'll also go if I can catch up in time!

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:52.440
Its acceleration is superb,
and it handles well.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:03.890
Lieutenant!

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:05.990
I apologize for my father's actions.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:08.020
There's nothing for you to apologize about.

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:10.420
I'm the one who should be chasing him!

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.730
Can you fire at your own father?

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.000
Stop it!

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:18.440
Let go of me!

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:23.440
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:25.500
You're not ready!

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:26.410
Let me go!

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:28.270
Astonaige, hang on there!

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:34.410
Lieutenant Franklin Bidan.
What a troublemaker he is...!

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:41.620
Are you sure?! We have no problem
catching up with him!

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:44.790
The Gundam Mk. II's acceleration
is excellent.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:48.030
However, personally, I'm rather
proud of Rick Dias.

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:49.400
Naturally.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:52.690
However, Franklin isn't
your average engineer.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.100
- Watch out.
- <i>Roger.</i>

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:03.670
Have you heard of the man
they called the Red Comet?

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:08.780
I was on the rear-guard ship Salamis
during the A Baoa Qu battle.

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:09.840
I see.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:12.620
But I never saw that Zeong.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:18.220
However, I did sense the power of
the Red Comet.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:20.790
I'm getting that feeling now.

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:22.030
From who?

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.660
Lieutenant Quattro Bajeena.

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:24.900
I see.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:30.500
He is trying to convey Zeon Deikun's
dying wishes to us Spacenoids.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:34.580
Kamille! Where are you going?!

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:37.870
I can't forgive my father
for going to Green Noa to see his lover.

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:39.280
A lover?

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:43.210
I can't trouble Lieutenant Quattro
with something like this.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.110
You're mistaken.

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:47.250
Your father is a very skilled technician...!

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:48.950
Stay out of this!

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:51.760
People like you who have lived
a fortunate life...

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:54.160
...cannot understand the position
of the child in this case!

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:12.280
They've begun the transfer, sir.

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:14.180
Space defense section reporting!

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:16.910
A number of unidentified spacecraft
are approaching!

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:18.880
- Any of our military units in that area?
- None, sir.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:21.120
Send out the Hizack team!

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:23.660
Fire one set thirty seconds from now...

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:26.700
...and order the Hizacks
to skirt around friendly fire!

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:27.730
Yes, sir.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:29.430
Also hurry with the transfer!

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:30.300
Yes, sir!

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:38.900
That seat's reserved for me.

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:41.040
Lieutenant Jerid! Are you sure about this?

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:44.780
Lieutenant Commander Jamaican has
given me a chance to redeem my honor.

00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:48.120
Sorry.

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:52.550
All units, launch as soon as you're ready.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:00.760
If I can improve my combat record,
the rest will fall into place.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:15.010
That's strange, the Alexandria should
be in sight by now.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:17.670
Where is it? Did I take the wrong course?

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:22.910
Impressive.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:32.360
What?!

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:37.930
- <i>Let go!</i>
- Give it up.

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:52.880
Hit confirmed.

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:53.880
I've detected the enemy!

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:03.420
How fortunate that I can test a machine
I designed in an actual battle...

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:05.590
...using the enemy's mobile suit.

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:12.730
<i>No engineer can be luckier!</i>

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:16.740
They're fighting among themselves?

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:21.740
This is how it's normally done!

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:27.810
Stop the unloading of goods at once.

00:11:27.890 --> 00:11:29.350
I'm boarding the Brunei.

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:31.010
<i>Captain, it's too dangerous now.</i>

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:33.490
We haven't entered the combat zone yet.

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:35.920
In the worst case, we can
evade them together with the Brunei.

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:37.160
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:43.590
Enemy vessel approaching!

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:46.760
We'll fire some feint shots
to shift the enemy's attention here!

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:49.200
Do you hear me?! Open fire!

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:57.280
They'll find out our position!

00:11:57.620 --> 00:12:00.020
Do not fire until Captain Bask
reaches the Brunei!

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:17.130
Who's there?!

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:20.530
Haven't you received the orders
to send out all available units?

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.970
What? But I've removed
the left arm of this Gundam!

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:25.530
I can use the rifle!

00:12:27.650 --> 00:12:29.110
It's not safe without the shield.

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:30.970
Astonaige! Stop him!

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:32.250
It's Kamille!

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:33.280
Kamille?

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:40.190
We'll fire another round,
then change our position!

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:47.820
Damn Blex!

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:50.060
It can't be helped!
Captain, we must return fire!

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:51.370
Fire!

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:13.280
I'm opening the hatch
to the mobile suit deck!

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:15.150
Lieutenant Reccoa!
You're out of your mind!

00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:18.550
We've got no choice!
But I think that child can pull it off!

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.590
We're in the midst of a battle
with an enemy vessel!

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:22.290
Kamille is a strong boy!

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:23.330
I understand!

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:27.370
Open hatch!
Mk. II, don't forget your rifle!

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:30.370
- Roger!
- <i>Kamille? What are you doing in Unit 1?!</i>

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:32.270
Voice circuit damaged!

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:37.610
Catapult! Ready to launch!

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:43.050
What did you say?! Kamille's piloting
a Mk. II that's partially disassembled?!

00:13:43.390 --> 00:13:46.360
Never mind! This'll be the perfect chance
to test his aptitude.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:49.390
Gundam Mk. II, Kamille, let's do it!

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:00.570
<i>Why did you have to go after</i>
<i>some young woman?!</i>

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:03.040
<i>How dare you hurt my mom</i>
<i>and go for a younger woman?!</i>

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:06.780
Kamille! Keep your cool when fighting!

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:17.410
This is war.

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:22.580
Captain Bask has boarded safely.

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:27.130
We should at least be grateful
that the Captain was not on the bridge.

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:28.920
Damage report!

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:31.090
We're transferring the command team
to the second bridge!

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:34.030
Okay! Everyone, transfer immediately
to the second bridge!

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:35.830
Have all artillery sections return fire!

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:53.320
There you are, dad!

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:03.200
I'm beginning to believe in
divine intervention! Lieutenant!

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:08.170
<i>You are pathetic!</i>

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:09.210
Kamille?!

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:22.140
Are you going to fire at your own father?!

00:15:29.890 --> 00:15:31.520
Pointing a gun at your own father?!

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:33.560
I don't remember raising you that way!

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:36.100
I've been fulfilling my obligation as a parent!

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:39.460
Yet, this is how you thank me
for all I've done for you?!

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:41.500
But you never understood me!

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:45.230
But you...!

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:54.380
Don't come!

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:57.110
Stop it!

00:15:57.590 --> 00:15:59.560
What's the big deal
with the Gundam Mk. II?!

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:01.450
I'm thinking ahead to the next one.

00:16:01.530 --> 00:16:05.360
And it won't... it won't be defeated
by that thing!

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:10.330
Dad! Calm down!

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:23.970
<i>Any hesitation could mean your life!</i>

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:25.380
<i>This is a battlefield!</i>

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:26.670
Who is it?!

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:49.560
You fool!

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:02.040
Wh-Where is it?!

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:11.760
An order to retreat?

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:16.360
I could redeem my honor
if only I was given a chance!

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:18.160
But I don't want to get lost!

00:17:25.280 --> 00:17:27.900
Because you do stuff like this,
everyone ends up dead!

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:33.110
If you guys stayed away
none of this would've happened!

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:37.810
<i>Kamille! Stop wasting ammunition!</i>

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:38.860
Lieutenant Quattro!

00:17:45.030 --> 00:17:47.000
<i>I'm heading to Green Noa.</i>

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:50.430
<i>I'm going to have Gryps hurry their</i>
<i>mobilization.</i>

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.020
<i>I'll leave the pursuit to you.</i>

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:53.090
Yes, sir!

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:57.460
Don't expect the so-called A.E.U.G.
secret base to be at Granada.

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:02.300
Assume that half of the Earth Federation
Forces' Space Army to be A.E.U.G..

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.750
The enemy appears to be chasing us
with three vessels.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:14.350
I doubt they can figure out our course
from this point on.

00:18:14.830 --> 00:18:16.790
It'll be difficult for them to attack us now.

00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:19.430
We'll skirt Luna II
and head for Earth!

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:22.160
All sections, damage report!

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:23.370
Yes sir!

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:24.630
Course set!

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:25.670
Destination, Earth!

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:30.330
It's nobody's fault.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:32.470
It was a battlefield out there.

00:18:32.680 --> 00:18:34.300
I...

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:35.940
...I tried to shoot down my father.

00:18:36.910 --> 00:18:40.710
Even if you hadn't,
someone eventually would have.

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:42.340
I'm coming in.

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:48.450
Lieutenant Emma,
it seems to fit you perfectly.

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:49.690
Thank you.

00:18:49.760 --> 00:18:53.890
I would've preferred to be enlisted,
as I'm still under probation.

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:55.790
I don't need you now.

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:57.830
I'll call you when the Lieutenant
is on the move again.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:58.870
Yes, sir!

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:03.240
Do you still think I'm a spy, Lieutenant?

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:05.070
Of course I do.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:10.050
As long as your parents live on Earth,
they're practically taken as hostages.

00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:12.810
There's always the possibility
of you returning to the Titans.

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:14.870
That's a realistic way
of looking at the situation.

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:16.750
That's right.

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:20.420
Just now, the enemy attacked
using a boy's parents as a shield.

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:23.190
And we are with the boy who's been
fighting against the enemy.

00:19:24.190 --> 00:19:25.720
That's what I came here to talk about.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:33.100
My parents are people with high ambitions.

00:19:33.170 --> 00:19:36.260
I'm sure that they would
understand my actions and forgive me.

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:39.910
That's great. How wonderful.

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:41.440
Kamille.

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:46.270
You're fortunate to have adults who...

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:47.750
...act like real parents,
Lieutenant Emma.

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:51.080
But Kamille, your parents also...

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:55.250
Those people are not parents!
They can't be!

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:56.290
Kamille!

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:59.590
Am I wrong to say such a thing?

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:03.260
But I wanted my parents
to be more like normal parents!

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:07.260
Is it wrong for a child to say that?!

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:10.700
My dad had a lover for quite some time...

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:14.540
...but my mom was so preoccupied
with her work...

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:17.380
...that she never paid attention to my
dad at all.

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:19.470
Is military work really that important?!

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:23.440
This isn't about the A.E.U.G. or the Titans.

00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:26.780
I can't stand to be always ignored
just because I'm a kid!

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:29.850
I understand what you're saying, but...!

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:33.030
Are you telling me
not to talk about my dead parents?

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:35.090
That's right.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:39.190
And you must create a better world for
the next generation of children.

00:20:39.270 --> 00:20:41.460
I take no such responsibility!

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:42.760
Yes, you do.

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:44.470
Who do you think you are,
Lieutenant?!

00:20:45.980 --> 00:20:48.500
I saw both of my parents being killed
right in front of my eyes!

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:51.550
There's no one with the right to say
anything about me and my parents!

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:55.980
Do you know of a man
by the name of Char Aznable?

00:20:57.590 --> 00:20:59.020
I respect him highly!

00:20:59.090 --> 00:21:02.150
That man took on the tragedy
of his parents all on his own...

00:21:02.230 --> 00:21:04.320
...and challenged the Zabi family.

00:21:06.130 --> 00:21:11.160
But he was a foolish man who retaliated
against that organization all on his own.

00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:14.300
That is an accurate comment.

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:19.400
However, judging from your words, you
would listen to what he might say, right?

00:21:19.810 --> 00:21:20.780
Lieutenant Quattro?

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.400
There's no chance of meeting him,
is there?!

00:21:23.480 --> 00:21:26.810
That man's position
is very similar to yours, Kamille.

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:30.520
He felt that expressing
his own individual emotions...

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:35.350
...was the most important thing
to overcome in the situation.

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:37.660
I don't want to hear this!

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:41.860
I told you the A.E.U.G. and Titans
mean nothing to me!

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:45.230
My parents were foolish enough to lose
their lives...

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:47.240
...amidst circumstances created by adults.

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:50.210
But still, they were my parents!

00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:51.710
Kamille!

00:21:56.450 --> 00:22:00.380
That wasn't too clever, raising that
subject to try to persuade him.

00:22:03.720 --> 00:22:05.280
You're right.

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:11.190
Regular folks like me have a bad habit
of wanting to tell others...

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:12.420
...of the various people they know.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:46.670 --> 00:23:50.690
The Argama must send
Reccoa Londe down to Earth.

00:23:50.770 --> 00:23:54.400
Seeing this as an opportunity to attack,
Lila and Jerid plan an assault.

00:23:55.370 --> 00:23:56.860
"I want to protect that person."

00:23:57.510 --> 00:24:01.740
That sudden impulse takes Kamille
into a battle affected by Earth's gravity.

00:24:02.620 --> 00:24:06.850
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"To Earth".

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
To Earth

00:24:07.490 --> 00:24:09.820
You will see the tears of time.
